replace('AASLD 2023 and OPTN policy allow the standardized exception after an AFP above 1,000 falls below 500 ng/mL following treatment.','OPTN policy uses AFP above 1,000 followed by reduction below 500 ng/mL after treatment; AASLD’s guidance uses 1,000 or more. The current OPTN policy governs standardized exception scoring, which is distinct from listing.','B11-R13-CF13',src,'hcc')
replace('Like OPTN, supports the standardized exception after an AFP above 1,000 falls below 500 ng/mL following treatment.','Uses AFP ≥1,000 followed by a reduction below 500 ng/mL after treatment; OPTN policy itself uses >1,000 for the standardized exception. Verify and apply the current policy operator.','B11-R13-CF13',src,'hcc')
qfield('hcc','HCC-D11','question','Agree the local AFP approach while distinguishing OPTN exception scoring (>1,000 then <500 after treatment), AASLD guidance (≥1,000) and the EASL downstaging condition (<1,000 for at least three months).','B11-R13-CF13',src)
qfield('hcc','HCC-D11','divergence','OPTN standardized exception policy, AASLD guidance and EASL clinical selection wording differ. Exception priority, waitlist registration and any stricter OPEN local proposal are separate decisions.','B11-R13-CF13',src)
qfield('hcc','HCC-D11','rationale','Apply current OPTN policy to standardized exception scoring: AFP >1,000 requires reduction below 500 after treatment. AASLD uses ≥1,000, while EASL requires AFP <1,000 for at least three months after downstaging. Record the source and purpose of each threshold; do not convert an OPEN local AFP proposal into automatic delisting.','B11-R13-CF13',src)
