src=B+'B11_hcc_roadmap/reviews/R13/R13_REPORT.md CF06; EASL2025 and current StageB per-session assessment'
replace('or persistent viable disease after two well-executed sessions — unless a specific curative or downstaging rationale remains and is recorded.','or inadequate response despite technically adequate treatment, assessed after each session. After one or two consecutive treatments without response, consider alternatives in MDT; document any reason to continue a curative or downstaging strategy.','B11-R13-CF06',src,'hcc')
replace('or persistent viable disease after two well-executed sessions unless a curative or downstaging rationale is recorded (a trigger the stage B note says v0.8 withdrew);','or inadequate response after technically adequate treatment, assessed after each session; continued treatment needs a recorded goal and rationale;','B11-R13-CF06',src,'hcc')
replace('Within the roadmap, the stop/switch card keeps persistent viability after two well-executed sessions as a switch trigger, while stage B and the limited-evidence table record that v0.8 withdrew the fixed two-session rule for per-session reassessment.','Use per-session multidisciplinary reassessment; the guidance’s one-or-two nonresponse signal prompts consideration of alternatives rather than an automatic treatment-count rule.','B11-R13-CF06',src,'hcc')
replace('The two-session TACE stop rule and what counts as ‘well executed’.','Per-session TACE response and reserve review, including what counts as technically adequate treatment.','B11-R13-CF06',src,'hcc')
replace("v0.8 withdrew the fixed two-session rule for reassessment after each session in MDT context, yet the stop/switch card still lists persistent viability after two well-executed sessions as a switch trigger; 'well executed' is undefined.",'Assess response, technical adequacy, hepatic reserve and treatment intent after each session; define these inputs locally rather than using a mandatory session count.','B11-R13-CF06',src,'hcc')
