replace('the Milan consensus records no benefit in the perihilar subgroup','Milan recommends adjuvant capecitabine or S-1 despite imprecise perihilar-specific estimates','B12-R12-F03',src,'hilar')
field('hilar','gates/5/crit/0','Unresectable disease outside the standardized transplant route, for example regional nodal disease or radial mass ≥3 cm. Regional nodes or size alone do not exclude resection: if otherwise resectable, return to resection assessment; confirm transplant measurements with the team.','B12-R12-F01',src)
replace('Regional nodal disease goes to neoadjuvant chemotherapy and then resection in responders, recognizing that a survival benefit is not established.','Otherwise resectable disease with regional nodes remains eligible for upfront resection and regional lymphadenectomy. A neoadjuvant-first approach is an OPEN trial/registry proposal that departs from Milan recommendation 53; its survival benefit is unestablished.','B12-R12-F02',src,'hilar')
replace('Regional nodes: FDG-PET-positive or tissue-proven regional nodes → neoadjuvant chemotherapy, restaging, resection if no distant disease.','Regional nodes: do not use FDG uptake alone to mandate neoadjuvant treatment. Review tissue confirmation when it changes treatment; upfront resection with lymphadenectomy remains the guideline route when otherwise resectable. Neoadjuvant-first treatment requires an explicitly approved trial or registry protocol.','B12-R12-F02',src,'hilar')
